{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1516193-some-aspects-of-the-game-are-actively-hurting-the-adventure-possibilities","id":1516193,"title":"Some aspects of the game are actively hurting the adventure possibilities.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-26T03:32:05-07:00","id":1516193,"title":"Some aspects of the game are actively hurting the adventure possibilities.","content":"Le Salon Des Femmes Nouveaux, The Order of the Stars and, to a lesser extent then the previous two, The Archivists are all Allegiances that got ear marked for being amongst <i>the</i> playable factions and they are all incredibly narrow in their focus. These are not pulp-y groups that have a thematically coherent thread binding them together, they are ideologically motivated groups with very specific goals. I really think it does the setting a disservice.<br /> <br /> I know the other factions have their own specific goals, but they are also immediately evocative of specific archetypes. Branch 9 = Spy, Air Circus = Heroic Pilot, that kind of thing. There should have been more factions like that. The Core Book did a good job of making Allegiances that fit that mold, but this book is really getting caught up in the game developers own preferred politics. Why no Reformed Big Game Hunters organization? Or a group of Occultists who believe that Telluric energy is magic? Maybe a group of modern day Knights that recruit from people all over the world? You can still have these politics and, at the same time, have a diverse group of exciting Allegiances that players can choose from, rather than three flavors of essentially the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T18:11:14-07:00","id":1516394,"title":"","content":"I totally disagree. I like all three of those Allegiances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T22:56:04-07:00","id":1518002,"title":"","content":"What would you use them for? Specifically to play a game about advancing social issues? How would you use them for a more general adventure?<br /> <br /> I personally really feel the lack of the Ponatowski Foundation as a playable faction. I'm guessing it's lack is due to some desire to keep players from being guilty of imperialism or colonialism associated with the organization, but that lack does away with some juicy potential drama. Indiana Jones I can picture working with the Ponatowski Foundation. He worked for Walter Donovan, a traitor who worked with fascists. You could easily have the organization split in an ideological civil war with PCs being involved with the good part of the allegiance. The Archivist could have been one part of that good part of the Foundation.<br /> <br /> The core book did have LRE which was reminiscent of the allegiances in Adventure, but they were a minor faction with most of the other factions actually concerned with facilitating adventure storytelling rather than political messaging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T23:17:36-07:00","id":1518006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1516193-some-aspects-of-the-game-are-actively-hurting-the-adventure-possibilities?p=1518002#post1518002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally really feel the lack of the Ponatowski Foundation as a playable faction. I'm guessing it's lack is due to some desire to keep players from being guilty of imperialism or colonialism associated with the organization, but that lack does away with some juicy potential drama. Indiana Jones I can picture working with the Ponatowski Foundation. He worked for Walter Donovan, a traitor who worked with fascists. You could easily have the organization split in an ideological civil war with PCs being involved with the good part of the allegiance. The Archivist could have been one part of that good part of the Foundation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also a bit sad <b><i>Pontowski Foundation</i></b> as both Center Europe and Poland related faction. Other Allegiances are good in my mind - just sad they did not put this Indiana Jones-like Center Europe group... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T23:22:22-07:00","id":1518007,"title":"","content":"The Foundation also has a built in storyline for players to try to get rid of the rot in the organization. It's a real mystery why they were cut out. They should have at least been a minor Allegiance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T05:06:25-07:00","id":1518024,"title":"","content":"Nothing's stopping you from making them a playable faction. Do the work yourself if you feel the game is missing something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","user":"NullApostle","date":". 07-16-2023, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T14:24:26-07:00","id":1518085,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of players would want them as an option, so there should have been rules for playing them provided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T16:12:56-07:00","id":1518098,"title":"","content":"Make them, write a Nexus product with them and sell them. If you think people will like it and buy it, it\u2019s probably true\u2026 I know I will buy and at least 50+ people will.<br /> <br /> There are lots of great material in the nexus and I suggest everyone to build their own books and sell them, it\u2019s amazing how it can add good material to the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T04:43:57-07:00","id":1518143,"title":"","content":"To make the Ponatowksi Foundation Path you'd probably just have to reskin the Global Cartography Initiative Path (from Core) a little bit. Very little effort required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T19:07:51-07:00","id":1518162,"title":"","content":"That's true. But that, in itself, makes me question why the Ponatowski Foundation was given the ax when the essentially reskinned modern version of the Allegiance was considered fine for the modern era. Hell, the modern era would have more reason to be sensitive about such issues, while the pulp Adventure era would be more forgiving of the kind of adventuring archeology that might be considered problematic in the current era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T14:16:55-07:00","id":1518203,"title":"","content":"In 1E the Ponatowski Foundation was a front for several villains as I recall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T17:40:00-07:00","id":1518207,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not sure why it wasn\u2019t included in Adventure! for SPCs and villains, but I definitely wouldn\u2019t make the Ponatowski Foundation a PC Allegiance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 07-18-2023, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T10:24:43-07:00","id":1518255,"title":"","content":"Why not? The Teragen is a player faction and they can be anything between people who simply believe that Nova's are fundamentally different from, and should be treated different to, baseline humanity and Nova supremacist terrorists.<br /> <br /> An Allegiance that has both heroic scholars going on adventures and shadowy individuals pulling their strings and slipping their own agents into the group seems cool. The heroic PC of the Ponatowski Foundation would be like Indiana Jones working for Walter Donovan. The Ponatowski Foundation could be either a protagonist or an antagonist faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T04:34:19-07:00","id":1519839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1516193-some-aspects-of-the-game-are-actively-hurting-the-adventure-possibilities?p=1518098#post1518098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make them, write a Nexus product with them and sell them. If you think people will like it and buy it, it\u2019s probably true\u2026 I know I will buy and at least 50+ people will.<br /> <br /> There are lots of great material in the nexus and I suggest everyone to build their own books and sell them, it\u2019s amazing how it can add good material to the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to ask, what\u2019s the Nexus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T06:08:55-07:00","id":1519855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1516193-some-aspects-of-the-game-are-actively-hurting-the-adventure-possibilities?p=1519839#post1519839\" r